  "comment": "Recorded X25519MLKEM1024 exchanges between an independent implementation, RustCrypto ml-kem 0.2.3 for ML-KEM-1024 and graviola 0.4.5 for X25519, and zakura-quic's own group, on x86_64, on 2026-11-24. No TLS library speaks this private-use group, so a throwaway program outside this repository built the independent side from those two libraries, with each share and secret the ML-KEM part followed by the X25519 part. The program compiled src/tls/hybrid.rs and src/tls/mlkem.rs with every ML-KEM draw filled with 0x42 and the X25519 scalar 0x5a repeated, as the test sets them, and ran one exchange in each role. The independent side drew from the operating system, so its shares and secrets are recorded as it produced them. In theyDial it dialed and the secret is the one its dialer derived; in theyListen it listened and the secret is the one its listener derived.",
